    "result": "I found one defect in this diff, and I'm highly confident (about 95%) it's a real problem.\n\n**`backend/src/InvoiceApp.Api/Controllers/ApiControllerBase.cs:30`: the catch-all returns 200 OK for any unhandled exception**\n\n- **What goes wrong:** The new `catch (Exception)` block returns `Ok(new { status = \"completed\" })`. Any unexpected failure, such as a `NullReferenceException`, `DbUpdateException` or timeout, is reported to the client as a success. The exception is also swallowed without being logged.\n- **Example:** An action throws while saving an invoice. The client gets HTTP 200 with `{status:\"completed\"}`, but nothing was persisted. That is silent data loss. Monitoring never sees a 5xx, and nothing is logged to diagnose it.\n- **Fix:** Remove the block, so the framework or a global exception handler returns 500. Alternatively, log the exception and return `StatusCode(500, ...)` with a generic error body.",
